      <Docs>
        <summary>
            A callback used to validate a client certificate when <see cref="P:Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Transport.DirectTls.DirectTlsEndpointOptions.ClientCertificateMode" /> requests one.
            Return <see langword="true" /> to accept the certificate. When not set, a certificate is accepted only
            when it produced no <see cref="T:System.Net.Security.SslPolicyErrors" />.
            </summary>
        <value>To be added.</value>
        <remarks>
            The callback is invoked on the <see cref="T:System.Threading.ThreadPool" />, so a slow one does not hold up the handshakes or
            I/O of other connections. It does still delay this connection, and the time spent in it counts against
            <see cref="P:Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Transport.DirectTls.DirectTlsEndpointOptions.HandshakeTimeout" /> - a callback that overruns that budget costs this connection its handshake.
            Prefer fast, non-blocking work regardless: each concurrent invocation occupies a thread-pool thread.
            </remarks>
      </Docs>
    </Member>
